---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { href } from '../data/site';
const questions = [
  { slug: 'cleansing', label: 'Bathing & cleansing', title: 'Does your whole body need soap every day?', text: 'Separate bathing, cleansing, and scrubbing. Then ask which parts you actually need.' },
  { slug: 'microbiome', label: 'Your microbiome', title: 'Who else is living on your skin?', text: 'A living ecosystem, a protective barrier, and a better question than “kill all the germs.”' },
  { slug: 'scent', label: 'Scent & diet', title: 'Can you eat your way to a better smell?', text: 'A small study, a big internet claim, and what your armpits actually tell us.' },
  { slug: 'natural', label: 'Natural & synthetic', title: 'Is natural always the gentler option?', text: 'Botanical fragrances, bath additives, and the trouble with a very persuasive label.' },
  { slug: 'useful-products', label: 'Products with a purpose', title: 'Which products earn their place?', text: 'Sun protection, moisturizers, and treatments deserve a fair hearing.' },
  { slug: 'hair', label: 'Hair & hydration', title: 'A simpler routine. Even for curls?', text: 'Less scrubbing, thoughtful conditioning, and no one-size-fits-all schedule.' },
];
---
<Layout title="Less product. More you.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">An independent inquiry into doing less</span>
        <h1>Less product.<br />More <em>you.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">Your skin doesn’t need a 12-step identity crisis. Could less lather, less scrubbing, and fewer products make everyday care simpler? Let’s follow the evidence.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-dark" href={href('research/')}>Question the routine</a><a class="text-link fine" href={href('why/')}>The idea behind it</a></div>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-art">
        <div class="hero-sticker" aria-hidden="true">100%<strong>human.</strong>pores included.</div>
        <img src={href('images/bath.webp')} width="1100" height="825" alt="A happy peach-colored character relaxing in a lilac bathtub and giving a peace sign." fetchpriority="high" />
        <figcaption class="hero-caption">Artist’s impression of having fewer things to think about.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="ticker"><div class="wrap ticker-inner"><span>Pro-curiosity</span><span class="ticker-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span>Less marketing. More evidence.</span><span class="ticker-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span>Comfortable in your own skin</span><span class="ticker-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span></div></div>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap intro-grid">
    <div><span class="eyebrow mb-5">The very serious question behind the joke</span><h2>What if we don’t<br />need all this stuff?</h2></div>
    <div class="intro-copy"><p>A daily shower can come with a whole ritual: soap everywhere, an exfoliating cloth, and another product to smooth things out. Which parts are doing useful work?</p><p>Free the Pores asks how far we can simplify that ritual while caring for the skin barrier and the life on it. Keep useful hygiene. Investigate the rest. Absolutely no checkout cart.</p><a class="text-link fine inline-block mt-5" href={href('about/')}>Read our ground rules</a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section questions"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Start with a question</span><h2>Let’s get under the surface.</h2></div><a class="text-link fine shrink-0" href={href('research/#library')}>Browse the source library</a></div>
    <div class="question-grid">{questions.map((question, i) => <a class="question-card" href={href(`research/${question.slug}/`)}><div class="question-top"><span class="question-number">0{i + 1}</span><span class="pill">{question.label}</span></div><h3>{question.title}</h3><p>{question.text}</p><span class="question-bottom">Explore the evidence</span></a>)}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section story-band"><div class="wrap story-grid">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">The idea behind the name</span><h2 class="big-quote mt-5">Your skin is a habitat.<br />Treat it like one.</h2><p class="fine">A living surface. A simpler approach.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Care for what’s already there.</h3><p>Skin has its own barrier and resident microbial communities. We want to understand how a routine can support them with fewer unnecessary steps.</p><p>Wash your hands. Question the automatic all-over lather. And ask what “a healthy microbiome” actually means.</p><a class="button" href={href('why/')}>Explore the idea</a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">A few things we’re clear about</span><h2>Small routine. Open mind.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="mini-grid"><article><span class="eyebrow">01 / Keep what helps</span><h3>Products can earn a place.</h3><p>Sunscreen, a moisturizer for dry skin, or a prescribed treatment can serve a real purpose. The evidence belongs in the conversation.</p><a class="text-link fine inline-block mt-4" href={href('research/useful-products/')}>See what holds up</a></article><article><span class="eyebrow">02 / Skip the purity contest</span><h3>Natural is not a safety test.</h3><p>Water and plant extracts are made of chemicals, too. A useful question is how a particular ingredient behaves at a particular dose, on your skin.</p><a class="text-link fine inline-block mt-4" href={href('research/natural/')}>Unpack the label</a></article><article><span class="eyebrow">03 / Stay curious</span><h3>A hypothesis deserves a test.</h3><p>Could a much simpler routine work for more people? We’re interested in comfort, skin health, and evidence that could change our minds.</p><a class="text-link fine inline-block mt-4" href={href('about/')}>How we read research</a></article></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section bottom-cta"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">No starter kit required</span><h2>Make some room<br />on the bathroom shelf.</h2><p>Consider what you wash, how much you scrub, and which products have a clear job. Simpler can start with one change.</p><a class="button button-dark" href={href('less/')}>Explore a simpler routine</a></div></section>
</Layout>
